    @* Start Section description*@
    <div class="container-fluid">
        <div class="col-md-3"></div>
        <div class="col-md-6 " style="text-align:justify;font-size:18px;">
            <h1 style="font-weight:bold;font-size:2em">Green Afghanistan</h1>
            <h1 style="font-weight:bold;font-size:1em">Planting Hope and Sustainability</h1>
            <p>Green Afghanistan, an initiative dedicated to planting trees across Afghanistan. This endeavour combats deforestation, addresses soil erosion, enhances air quality, and fosters biodiversity, creating a more resilient environment for Afghan communities.</p>
            <p>
                <img src="~/Content/projects/green-afghanistan/green-afghanistan-1.jpg" style="width:100%" />
            </p>
            <p>In addition to environmental benefits, the programme offers significant socio-economic impacts. It creates job opportunities for locals, providing income and skill development. Trees also boost agricultural productivity and provide resources like fruit and firewood, improving food security and livelihoods. Supporting this programme through donations is a powerful way to contribute to a greener, healthier, and more sustainable future for Afghanistan. Your contributions enable Human Relief Mission to plant more trees, expand their environmental efforts, and ensure Afghan communities thrive in a balanced ecosystem.</p>

            @* Start Qoute Section*@
            <div class="" style="padding-bottom:50px;margin-top:30px;">

                <div class="quote-container col-md-12">
                    <span class="" style="font-size:4em;font-weight:bold">&lsquo;&lsquo;</span>
                    <p class="quote">
                        The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is none amongst the Muslims who plants a tree or sows seeds, and then a bird, or a person or an animal eats from it, but is regarded as a charitable gift for him”
                    </p>
                    <p class="">Hadith | Sahih al-Bukhari</p>
                </div>

            </div>
            @* End Qoute Section*@
            <p>&nbsp;</p>

            <h1 style="font-weight:bold;font-size:1em">Combating Deforestation and Soil Erosion</h1>
            <p>Deforestation in Afghanistan has led to significant soil erosion, reducing the land's fertility and increasing the risk of landslides and flooding. By planting trees, Green Afghanistan directly combats these challenges. Trees anchor the soil with their roots, reducing erosion and promoting healthier, more stable land. This foundational work is essential for restoring Afghanistan's natural landscapes and ensuring long-term environmental health.</p>

            <h1 style="font-weight:bold;font-size:1em">Enhancing Air Quality and Biodiversity</h1>
            <p>Trees are vital for enhancing air quality as they absorb carbon dioxide and release oxygen, helping to mitigate the effects of pollution. Additionally, they provide habitats for various species, fostering biodiversity. This increased biodiversity supports ecosystem resilience, ensuring that Afghan communities benefit from a balanced and healthy environment.</p>

            <h1 style="font-weight:bold;font-size:1em">Socio-Economic Benefits</h1>
            <p>Beyond environmental impacts, Green Afghanistan has profound socio-economic benefits. The program creates job opportunities for local residents, providing stable incomes and fostering skill development in areas such as forestry and environmental management. This employment not only supports families but also empowers communities with the skills needed for sustainable land management. </p>

            <p>
                <img src="~/assets/custom-image/11.jpg" style="width:100%;" />
            </p>
            <p style="font-size:14px;">
                Image: Human Relief Mission service for green Afghanistan
            </p>

            <h1 style="font-weight:bold;font-size:1em">Boosting Agricultural Productivity and Resources</h1>
            <p>Trees play a crucial role in boosting agricultural productivity. They improve soil health, enhance water retention, and provide shade for crops, leading to better yields. Additionally, many of the trees planted bear fruit, offering a valuable food source, and provide firewood, which is essential for cooking and heating. These resources directly contribute to improved food security and livelihoods for Afghan families.</p>
            
            <h1 style="font-weight:bold;font-size:1em">The Impact of Your Contributions</h1>
            <p>Supporting Green Afghanistan through donations is a powerful way to contribute to a greener, healthier, and more sustainable future for Afghanistan. Your contributions enable the Human Relief Mission to plant more trees, expand environmental efforts, and ensure Afghan communities thrive in a balanced ecosystem. Each tree planted is a step towards combating climate change, supporting biodiversity, and enhancing the socio-economic stability of Afghan communities.</p>
        </div>
